nebula compressor
==================

Write a function:

    def nebula_compressor(operation: str, data: str) -> str

Run-length encoding with two modes selected by `operation`:

  * "compress"   - collapse runs of the same character. A run of length 1
                   stays a single character; a run of 2..9 becomes the
                   character followed by its count; a run longer than 9 is
                   split into chunks of at most 9 (12 a's become "a9a3").
  * "decompress" - reverse the encoding: a character followed by a digit is
                   repeated that many times, any other character is copied
                   through unchanged.

Any other operation returns "Error". Empty data returns "".

Examples:
    nebula_compressor("compress", "aaabbbcccc") -> "a3b3c4"
    nebula_compressor("compress", "abc") -> "abc"
    nebula_compressor("compress", "aaaaaaaaaaaa") -> "a9a3"
    nebula_compressor("compress", "") -> ""
    nebula_compressor("decompress", "a3b3c4") -> "aaabbbcccc"
    nebula_compressor("decompress", "x") -> "x"
    nebula_compressor("explode", "abc") -> "Error"
